    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, Loyola College, Chennai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Singati2/topological-index-orthogonality"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "topological indices"
  - "degree-based indices"
  - "Sombor index"
  - "redundancy"
  - "partial correlation"
  - "QSPR"
  - "molecular descriptors"
abstract: >-
  Code, verified data and results for "Degree-Based Topological Indices Are
  Exactly Redundant on Molecular Data: A Span Certificate and a Target-Aware
  Screen for New Descriptors" (v2): a rank certificate under which every
  bond-incident-degree index is an exact linear combination of a classical
  baseline, a census of published Sombor-type and other degree-based indices
  on four MoleculeNet benchmarks, a target-aware screen with intervals and a
  cross-fitted non-linear check for non-degree-based candidates, and a
  graph-collision information ceiling with a graph-grouped benchmark.
version: "2.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
